0008: gen2 gets `has_generic_clear` and `QCTDD12766770_r8g8_fc_alignment`.

**Status:** shipped in `27.0.0-devel-p14`. Upstream: not sent - it flips two
device-table flags for gen2, and why upstream withholds them is not documented
here (the row names a Qualcomm erratum id, not a reason).
**Found:** 30.09, journal 15: of all gen2 properties, this is the only one with a
measurable effect.

## For users of other drivers

Nothing to set: the two flags live in the device table, not in a knob (the
measurement was done through `TU_FORCE_PROPS`, 0007).

## Summary

`has_generic_clear` makes "clear and draw" stop loading the previous render
target contents (generic clear disables conditional load/store,
`tu_pass.cc:560`); the erratum flag rides with it. On vkmark that is a 61-65 %
shorter frame in vertex/shading/texture; in RE4 it measured 0 %.

## Evidence

One hunk in the `a7xx_gen2` entry of `freedreno_devices.py`
(`QCTDD12766770 = True` and the generic-clear flag). Measurements: journal 15.2
(vkmark table), 15.3 (corruption check), 15.4 (RE4: no gain).

## Tests

| what the hunk changes | how it is checked | result |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| vkmark frame time | `results/vkmark-ab-combo.txt`, `vkmark-ab-r8g8.txt`, journal 15.2 | vertex -63.1 %, shading -61.1 %, texture -64.5 % |
| correctness | `results/test-props2-gc*.log` + `pixelcheck`, journal 15.3 | 94 PASS, byte-identical to base; 0-1 px of 880 |
| the title that matters | RE4, journal 15.4 | 0 % gain |

## The change in this repo

Two table rows, one hunk. It must not be read as "gen2 supports generic clear
everywhere": the corruption check is what backs it, and RE4 gives it nothing.
Revert: `git apply -R` with the file name explicit.

## Related

`0007` (the knob that measured it); ADR-0008 (no fps lever in the
driver for this title).

